---
import DocLayout from "../layouts/DocLayout.astro";
---

<DocLayout title="" description="Bazel build files, navigable in your editor">
  <header>
    <h1>bazel-language-server</h1>
    <code>//...</code>
  </header>

  <p>
    A language server for Bazel and Starlark. Navigate labels and <code
      >load()</code
    > paths, rename targets across packages, search the workspace, format and
    lint files, and build or test targets from your editor.
  </p>

  <p>
    It works from source alone. Bazel 8.0 or newer adds targets created by
    macros and correct external-repository resolution. Bazel 8.7 adds an exact
    native flag catalog for <code>*.bazelrc</code>. <code>buildifier</code> enables
    formatting and lint diagnostics for Starlark files.
  </p>

  <h2>Documentation</h2>

  <ul>
